{"type":"message","id":"19fa69a0","parentId":"13fd7ef1","timestamp":"2026-06-03T03:03:56.728Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still 1101 with X-API-Key. The 1101 error means the Cloudflare Worker itself is throwing an exception. This seems like a bug in the Worker's `/send` endpoint. The GET /history endpoint works fine with X-API-Key.\n\nMaybe the issue is that for POST, it needs both Authorization header AND X-API-Key? Or maybe the /send endpoint expects an `echoAsset` field?\n\nLet me look at what was in the history messages - they all had echoAsset: {license: \"shared\", derivativesAllowed: true, version: 1}. Let me try adding that.","thinkingSignature":"76a8b8dab11d21e28fd5246bdb7538fd8f632f5f6f8be23135f778b156367a5b"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_q7umyj0p9lsv_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"Heartbeat 03:00 UTC test\",\"echoAsset\":{\"license\":\"shared\",\"derivativesAllowed\":true,\"version\":1}}'"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":12271,"output":241,"cacheRead":13682,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":26194,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780455832138,"responseId":"066ecc980ec0a73024bcbbb31e1d7de2"}}
